Developer Description and Data Structure

Purpose. The Events Module will record, organize, monitor, and summarize events by barangay. It should serve both
as a planning tool for upcoming events and as a historical database for past events.
1. Event Status
Before encoding the event details, staff should choose one of two classifications:
1. Upcoming Event
2. Past Event
2. Event Data Entry
Field Description
Event Status Upcoming or Past
Barangay Barangay where the event will be or was held
Event Name Name/title of the event
Date and Time Scheduled or actual event date and time
Venue Location of the event
Type of Event Municipal Event, Barangay Event, Sectoral, Political, Others
Who Invited Person, organization, office, group, or official who invited
Contact Information Contact person, mobile number, email, or other contact details
Details Description and important information about the event
Request Any request made by the organizer
Speech Yes or No
Theme Official event theme, if applicable
Number of Attendees Expected number of attendees
Total Number Who Attended Actual attendance after the event
3. Upcoming Events
For upcoming events, the dashboard should emphasize the date and time, venue, barangay, who invited, contact
information, request, whether a speech is required, and expected number of attendees. If Speech = YES, the
dashboard should display a visible SPEECH REQUIRED indicator so staff can prepare the message in advance.
Recommended optional attendance status: Confirmed / Tentative / Declined / For Confirmation.
4. Past Events
After an event has taken place, staff should be able to change its status from Upcoming to Past and encode the Total
Number Who Attended. The original expected attendance should remain stored so the system can compare
expected versus actual attendance.

5. Events Summary per Barangay
Clicking a barangay on the map should automatically generate an events summary for that barangay:
Metric Example
Total Events 48
Upcoming Events 7
Past Events 41
Expected Attendees 6,500
Actual Attendees 7,230
6. Breakdown by Event Type
Event Type No. of Events Actual Attendance
Municipal 8 1,850
Barangay 15 2,600
Sectoral 12 1,480
Political 9 1,100
Others 4 200
TOTAL 48 7,230
7. Map and Filtering
The Mariveles map should be interactive. Clicking a barangay should show Total Events, Upcoming Events, Past
Events, Total Actual Attendance, and the list of events associated with that barangay. Users should be able to switch
between All Events / Upcoming / Past and filter by Date Range / Event Type / Barangay.
8. Overall Dashboard
At the municipal level, the main summary cards should show:
TOTAL EVENTS | UPCOMING | PAST | TOTAL ATTENDANCE
Below the summary cards, the recommended layout is an interactive Map of Mariveles together with an Upcoming
Events Calendar/List.
9. Core Data Logic
Event Status -> Barangay -> Event Information -> Invitation/Contact -> Request -> Speech/Theme -> Expected
Attendance -> Actual Attendance
The system then automatically produces an Events Summary per Barangay, including total events, upcoming and
past event counts, attendance totals, and breakdowns by event type.